msgstr "More than one language in one file"

#: ../../guide/languages.md:65
msgid "`engines.spell_language` is the document default, not the only answer. A thesis in French quoting English, or a German paper with an English abstract, is checked passage by passage: the prose is grouped by language and each group goes to the engines that read it, so Harper handles the English while LanguageTool handles the French."
msgstr "`engines.spell_language` is the document default, not the only answer. A thesis in French quoting English, or a German paper with an English abstract, is checked passage by passage: the prose is grouped by language and each group goes to the engines that read it, so Harper handles the English while LanguageTool handles the French."

#: ../../guide/languages.md:71
msgid "Three things declare a language, strongest first."
msgstr "Three things declare a language, strongest first."

#: ../../guide/languages.md:73
msgid "**A region directive.** Works in every format, and is the only option where the markup has nothing to say:"
msgstr "**A region directive.** Works in every format, and is the only option where the markup has nothing to say:"

#: ../../guide/languages.md:82
msgid "**A scope marker**, which runs until the next one:"
msgstr "**A scope marker**, which runs until the next one:"

#: ../../guide/languages.md:88
msgid "**The markup's own declaration**, where the format has one. Typst does:"
msgstr "**The markup's own declaration**, where the format has one. Typst does:"

#: ../../guide/languages.md:95
msgid "That last one needs no extra annotation at all — the `lang:` an author already writes for hyphenation and quotation marks is the one the checker reads, and `region:` becomes the BCP-47 subtag."
msgstr "That last one needs no extra annotation at all — the `lang:` an author already writes for hyphenation and quotation marks is the one the checker reads, and `region:` becomes the BCP-47 subtag."

